  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Add a way to see where the tracker balls will appear on your avatar in Unity before even going into VRChat.\nA way to add your real life height and calculate where everything will end up before putting on your tracker. Sometimes after working on the model, your legs are just  horribly misaligned with your virtual feet. Back to modeling, after I remove all my gear!\nI know some people wear the leg trackers differently. Some where them on the foot, and others on the ankle. There could be a setting to compensate for this minor change.\nAnd from experience, after resizing the head's viewpoint and shrinking the arms, I never really know how high off the foot the tracker is going to be when calibrating. It would simply make it a little easier when setting up. \n\"Oh, that's way off! I need to fix this before getting my gear on.\"",
